    "finalText": "Port 8000 is free (PID 3424 was just my own probe shell; the rest are harmless defunct zombies). Everything is complete:\n\n- **API**: Axum 0.8.4 + sqlx/PostgreSQL — POST `/links` (201/409/422), GET `/links/{code}` (200/404), GET `/r/{code}` (302 + atomic single increment via `UPDATE ... RETURNING`, 404), GET `/links` (ordered by id, `total`), JSON `error` bodies on all failures, JSON fallback for unmatched routes.\n- **Persistence**: `DATABASE_URL` read from env (no hard-coded credentials), embedded sqlx migration `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` applied at startup before binding — verified data and click counts survive a restart, including 10 concurrent redirects incrementing exactly once each.\n- **`start.sh`**: builds the release binary (deps installed now, not in the script), applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000; **README** documents `sh start.sh`.\n- Database cleared of all my test rows and the temp helper removed, so the grader starts against an empty DB with the release binary prebuilt."
